# CSV and TSV lexer lookup

## Root cause

The CSV and TSV lexer classes have aliases, but Pygments discovers third-party lexers through package entry points. The package registers only Carve, so a consumer calling `get_lexer_by_name` for either delimited language cannot find its lexer.

## Change

Register both existing classes in the `pygments.lexers` entry point group. Test lookup through Pygments and check that the separator receives a distinct operator token.

## Scope

Registration applies to every consumer that asks Pygments for these language names, independent of the fence content or host application. The lexer rules already handle the fields and separators.
